msgid "Элементы header"
msgstr "Header elements"

msgid ""
"Все три класса импортируются из ``bytespec``. Готовые экземпляры задаются в tuple ``__header__`` "
"при объявлении модели. Практическое руководство: :doc:`../headers`; наследование: "
":doc:`../inheritance`."
msgstr ""
"All three classes are imported from ``bytespec``. Instances are supplied in the ``__header__`` "
"tuple when declaring a model. Practical guide: :doc:`../headers`; inheritance: "
":doc:`../inheritance`."

msgid "Параметры"
msgstr "Parameters"

msgid ""
"Использует ``__constructor__`` (по умолчанию 1). При наличии этого элемента тип значения "
"проверяется при сборке модели, диапазон — при encode. ``include_constructor=False`` в encode и "
"``expect_constructor=False`` в decode_from полностью пропускают элемент; это не режим чтения без "
"проверки значения. Вложенные модели используют именно такой пропуск."
msgstr ""
"Uses ``__constructor__`` (1 by default). When this element is present, the value's type is "
"checked when building the model; its range is checked during encode. "
"``include_constructor=False`` in encode and ``expect_constructor=False`` in decode_from omit the "
"element entirely; this does not mean reading without validating the value. Nested models use this"
" same omission."

msgid ""
"Длина всех полей после полного header, исключая весь header, независимо от позиции элемента. Без "
"него decode_from возвращает конец известных полей и не задаёт отдельную границу body."
msgstr ""
"The length of all fields after the complete header, excluding the entire header, regardless of "
"the element's position. Without it, decode_from returns the end of the known fields and does not "
"establish a separate body boundary."

msgid ""
"Bitmap присутствующих optional-полей. ``Flags(1)`` вмещает биты 0–7, ``Flags(8)`` и "
"``Flags(VarUInt)`` — 0–63. При наличии optional-полей отсутствие этого элемента вызывает "
"SchemaError при объявлении класса, включая подклассы с унаследованными полями. См. :ref:`header-"
"validation`."
msgstr ""
"A bitmap of present optional fields. ``Flags(1)`` holds bits 0–7; ``Flags(8)`` and "
"``Flags(VarUInt)`` hold bits 0–63. If optional fields exist, omitting this element raises "
"SchemaError at class declaration, including in subclasses with inherited fields. See :ref"
":`header-validation`."

msgid ""
"Общий параметр ``encoding`` принимает ``1``, ``2``, ``4``, ``8`` (байты) или ``VarUInt`` из "
"``bytespec.types``. Другие encodings вызывают ``SchemaError``. Порядок байтов фиксированных "
"encodings задаёт модель."
msgstr ""
"The common ``encoding`` parameter accepts ``1``, ``2``, ``4``, ``8`` (bytes), or ``VarUInt`` from"
" ``bytespec.types``. Other encodings raise ``SchemaError``. The model sets the byte order for "
"fixed-width encodings."

msgid ""
"Эти элементы описывают вычисляемые и проверяемые служебные числа. Для пользовательских значений "
"header используйте вложенную модель; добавлять их через внутренние контексты сборки схемы не "
"требуется."
msgstr ""
"These elements describe computed and validated metadata numbers. Use a nested model for custom "
"header values; there is no need to add them through internal schema-building contexts."

msgid "Model identifier from **constructor**, validated during decoding."
msgstr "Model identifier from **constructor**, validated during decoding."

msgid "Unsigned integer width in bytes (1, 2, 4, 8) or VarUInt."
msgstr "Unsigned integer width in bytes (1, 2, 4, 8) or VarUInt."

msgid ""
"The int type is validated when building the schema; the value range is validated during encoding."
" Nested models skip this element."
msgstr ""
"The int type is validated when building the schema; the value range is validated during encoding."
" Nested models skip this element."

msgid "The size of all encoded fields, excluding the entire header."
msgstr "The size of all encoded fields, excluding the entire header."

msgid "The unsigned integer width in bytes (1, 2, 4, 8), or VarUInt."
msgstr "The unsigned integer width in bytes (1, 2, 4, 8), or VarUInt."

msgid ""
"When reading, bounds the field buffer by the declared length. The position of this element within"
" the header does not change the meaning of the stored number."
msgstr ""
"When reading, bounds the field buffer by the declared length. The position of this element within"
" the header does not change the meaning of the stored number."

msgid "A bitmap indicating the presence of optional fields, computed from their values."
msgstr "A bitmap indicating the presence of optional fields, computed from their values."

msgid ""
"A field is present if its value is not None. Bit numbers are set using field(flag=...) and are "
"limited to 0–63; with a fixed width, all used bits are checked to ensure they fit."
msgstr ""
"A field is present if its value is not None. Bit numbers are set using field(flag=...) and are "
"limited to 0–63; with a fixed width, all used bits are checked to ensure they fit."

